-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Dynamite Dan
  Publisher   Mirrorsoft, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Dynamite Dan (1985)(Mirrorsoft).z80
  MD5         3470d12b21edb24d6b665dfac5e8d84d

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.09% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, the default
              build (its keys code adds 3 T a tick); probe 0xC80A (the main
              loop, once a tick); input keyed to ticks; lockstep on lives and
              room; 10 trials per scene of up to 300 ticks (the mean; single
              trials -0.6 to +0.5 percent))

  Changes     1.0: Dan as Next sprites, the airship's hull and cables in front
              of him; Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt ROM, so the game
              starts from its own BASIC; the game's speed restored after every
              hook; R kept as the original's
              1.1: QUIT and PAUSE can be redefined (option, on by default)

  Note        Keys: a key on the loading screen, then ENTER on the menu. In
              play A left, S right, SPACE jump, P pause, Q quit. On by
              default, all five can be set on the game's own define-keys page
              (D on its menu), which now also asks for QUIT and PAUSE; the
              menu line "Original keys (Q,P fixed)" gives 1.0's game exactly.
              The "Disable Q quit key" cheat disables whichever key is set for
              QUIT. Dan is a bright cyan Next sprite over his own pixels, and
              in the airship room the hull and cables are drawn in front of
              him; rooms, enemies and panel keep the original's colours. It
              starts from the tape's own BASIC. Known issues: about 0.1 to 0.2
              percent slower than the original (the game has no padding to
              repay the hook from); once in a few hundred frames Dan's sprite
              is a frame ahead of his own pixels. Missing: no Enhanced colour
              set; five archive cheats (never shown to work, or ask for a
              value); the ending not reached in testing; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  No enemies
   3  Energy never decreases
   4  Disable Q quit key

  Cheats come from the archive's POKEs for this release.

